Drop ext/uri's hard module dependency on lexbor.

This firmware doesn't build lexbor (its ~370 KB of static tables overflow the ESP32's internal
RAM), so the WHATWG URL parser is stubbed and the lexbor module isn't registered. Without this,
uri_module_entry's ZEND_MOD_REQUIRED("lexbor") fails at startup, which cascades: ext/standard
requires uri, so the whole engine fails to start. ext/uri keeps the RFC 3986 (uriparser) and the
legacy parse_url() parsers, which is what the core stream layer uses.
diff --git a/ext/uri/php_uri.c b/ext/uri/php_uri.c
--- a/ext/uri/php_uri.c
+++ b/ext/uri/php_uri.c
@@ -46,7 +46,9 @@ static zend_object_handlers object_handlers_rfc3986_uri;
 static zend_object_handlers object_handlers_whatwg_uri;
 
 static const zend_module_dep uri_deps[] = {
-	ZEND_MOD_REQUIRED("lexbor")
+	/* php-baremetal: lexbor is not built (its static tables overflow the internal RAM), so drop the
+	 * hard dependency on the lexbor module. ext/uri keeps the RFC 3986 (uriparser) and legacy
+	 * parse_url() parsers; the WHATWG parser is stubbed (see compat/uri_whatwg_stub.c). */
 	ZEND_MOD_END
 };
 
